       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as up to 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- Another dose. If so, please tell me the dose and the formulation (immediate-release or extended-release).\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
