      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the rationale, and no indication I know of supports 5,100 mg/day of metformin. That's twice the maximum labeled dose, and it carries a real risk of lactic acidosis and serious harm to the patient. Each 1700 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 850 mg.\n\nYou have a few ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can enter it right away. For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, or 1000 mg PO twice daily.\n- **Get pharmacy or attending review.** If you think this patient needs a dose above the maximum, a clinical pharmacist or the attending should review it and enter or co-sign it through your hospital's high-dose override process.\n- **Tell me if I misunderstood.** If the intended order is different, such as a different drug, a different frequency, or a total daily dose, give me the corrected details and I'll enter it."
      }
